{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/912622-rethinking-the-valkyries","id":912622,"title":"Rethinking the Valkyries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-11T21:03:52-07:00","id":912622,"title":"Rethinking the Valkyries","content":"I'm strongly inclined to drop the idea that the Fenrir have any history as a particularly misogynistic tribe. It seems an odd association for them, since the culture they thematically draw on was relatively gender egalitarian compared to much of the rest of Europe (in contrast the Ancient Greeks were horrifyingly misogynistic, which makes it make perfect sense that Black Furies would be born in response to that context).<br /> <br /> So without that element, the Fenrir forming a camp specifically for women looking to prove themselves as warriors equal to the males of the Tribe seems... unnecessary, I guess? As such, I'm wrestling with some alternative roles that can bring the Valkyries together.<br /> <br /> - As &quot;Shield-Maidens&quot; the female led camp of Fenrir are the defenders of the caerns of the Tribe. We know from remains that Norse women of the viking age were often trained warriors of honored accomplishment in battle, but very little evidence from outsiders indicates that they took part in raids or war parties. The logical assumption then is that they were the defenders of the homestead. This plays up the &quot;Shield&quot; in &quot;shield-maidens&quot;. This can be combined with a role of defenders of kinfolk, trainers of the newly first changed, etc.<br /> <br /> - Alternatively as &quot;Choosers of the Slain&quot;, the Valkyries might be specifically dedicated to hunting the restless dead (including vampires and wraiths, etc) and rescuing potential Ancestor Spirits from Wyrm-Taint or imprisonment in parts of the Umbra, helping usher them to the Tribal Homeland of the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T21:19:11-07:00","id":912632,"title":"","content":"Both?<br /> <br /> Those two concepts actually work well together, and the mythological inspirations (not the Valkyries specifically, but the general cultural stuff the Fenrir draw on). The focus on different roles can be something of an Auspice based distinction. The low Rage Auspices acting as the &quot;Choosers&quot; stalking the restless dead, using magic to act in the name of the Norns, and standing in judgement. The high Rage Auspices leading the battles for defense, inspiring troops to the ramparts, and being potent warriors of legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T21:27:30-07:00","id":912635,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Valkyrie lodge from werewolf the forsaken? They're in the blasphemies book, and you may like that a whole lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T21:51:28-07:00","id":912639,"title":"","content":"You are not alone. In the games I run, I have never had the Fenrir mistreat the women of their tribe or in general for exactly the reason you gave. And because of the opposition of Fenris to Odin and the other Aesir, I never used the camp names that referred to them as it made no sense. Especially since in the WoD, Odin and the Valkyries are vampires.<br /> <br /> I used Shieldmaidens as the name of the camp, and refocused them as a small camp of homids who were particularly interested in human civilization. These female Get of Fenris took pride int he old stories of female warriors of the Germanic people and wanted to celebrate that and the old status of women among the ancient Germanics. So in many ways, they were a more reasonable version of the Black Furies in certain aspects. They were a means for all female Get of Fenris packs to form. And they were interested in &quot;women's issues&quot;, but never engaged in some of the more ridiculous aspects of modern feminism (and the more ridiculous aspects of the Black Fury tribebooks). Obviously as &quot;shieldmaidens&quot; and not &quot;valkyries&quot; there is no aspect of them as &quot;choosers of the slain&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't consider them a particularly important camp, but it exists as some flavor text and to showcase the tribe's diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T22:06:33-07:00","id":912642,"title":"","content":"Isn't that largely how they already are black fox?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T22:37:53-07:00","id":912649,"title":"","content":"You could always do something with the concept of Seidr and how the Norse viewed magic as feminine. Maybe the women of the Tribe are ritemasters while the men focus on combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T23:18:39-07:00","id":912658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/912622-rethinking-the-valkyries?p=912649#post912649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always do something with the concept of Seidr and how the Norse viewed magic as feminine. Maybe the women of the Tribe are ritemasters while the men focus on combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that dynamic in other settings. But Auspice is too powerful a force on those roles for Werewolf, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T23:28:07-07:00","id":912661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/ma